INT. SUBMERGED CHAPEL - NIGHT

A drowned stone nave, half-flooded after a dam failure. Waist-deep black water. Pews float like wreckage. Flashlights stab the dark, throwing wavering circles on vaulted arches overhead. Water drips from a hole in the roof.

DETECTIVE IRENE KASPRZAK (40s, waders, a tight jaw) wades down the aisle. Behind her, FORENSIC TECH BASIL NWOSU (30s, a camera held overhead) picks his way through floating hymnals. A third figure, a local priest, FATHER ANSELMO DURAN (60s, black cassock hitched to his knees), carries a lantern, mumbling prayers.

IRENE
Basil, light.

BASIL
Coming.

ANSELMO
Detective, this is a consecrated place.

IRENE
It's a crime scene, Father.

BASIL
Both can be true.

ANSELMO
Not tonight.

A ripple spreads from the altar. All three stop.

IRENE
Stay behind me.

ANSELMO
(over Irene)
It's only the dam still settling, it does that --

BASIL
(over Anselmo)
Those are footprints, Irene. Look, on the altar step. Wet.

IRENE
Fresh?

BASIL
Minutes.

ANSELMO
Impossible. No one has been in here since the flood.

IRENE
Somebody has.

She raises her flashlight. The beam finds the altar, then a dark shape slumped behind it. Water drips from a gloved hand.

IRENE (CONT'D)
Police! Show me your hands!

Nothing. Then the hand slowly moves, and a small hoarse sound croaks out of the dark.

ANSELMO
(a whisper)
Dear God. He's alive.

Anselmo drops the lantern. It hisses out in the water. The chapel plunges into black.
